From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WGpuFury <wgpufury@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement futures, WaitAny and the remaining unimplemented
 functions

- WGPUFuture registry honoring WGPUCallbackMode (WaitAnyOnly, AllowProcessEvents,
  AllowSpontaneous; an unset mode keeps the old fire-immediately behavior).
- wgpuInstanceWaitAny, including timed waits (WGPUInstanceFeatureName_TimedWaitAny,
  timedWaitAnyMaxCount = 64), and wgpuInstanceProcessEvents firing callbacks.
- Pending callbacks fire with CallbackCancelled when the instance is released.
- wgpuDeviceGetLostFuture; the lost callback also fires on wgpuDeviceDestroy, on
  release, and with FailedCreation when wgpuAdapterRequestDevice fails.
- wgpuDeviceCreateComputePipelineAsync / wgpuDeviceCreateRenderPipelineAsync.
- wgpuGetProcAddress (table generated by build.rs from the headers).
- wgpuGetInstanceFeatures, wgpuHasInstanceFeature, wgpuSupportedInstanceFeaturesFreeMembers.
- wgpuBufferReadMappedRange / wgpuBufferWriteMappedRange; Get(Const)MappedRange
  return NULL on error instead of aborting.
- wgpuTextureGetTextureBindingViewDimension.
- WGPUErrorFilter_Internal and WGPUErrorType_Internal; popping an empty error scope
  reports WGPUPopErrorScopeStatus_Error instead of aborting.
- Uncaptured errors and device loss without a callback are logged, not fatal.
